course: dictionary
lesson: 506
title: Big words in big news
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An assassination is the murder of an important or famous person, such as a leader, usually for political reasons. The word is about one person being killed on purpose, and that person is usually well known.
explain: Read the clues around the word. In «The assassination changed world events», the words changed world events tell you this was very big news, so the person was important.
explain: Notice the phrases that go with it. An «assassination attempt» is a try to murder an important person, and an «assassination plot» is a secret plan to do it. «"Wet work" means assassination» is slang that you may meet in spy stories.
fact: Assassination is a noun: an assassination, assassinations.
fact: «Assassination» means the murder of an important or famous person, usually for political reasons.
fact: Some assassinations changed world events, and one helped start a great war in Europe.
fact: «Assassination attempt» means a try to murder an important person.
fact: «Wet work» is slang that means assassination.
exercise: What does assassination mean? | *The murder of an important or famous person | A quiet walk in a park | A kind of election | A birthday party for a famous person
exercise: What does «assassination plot» mean? | A new kind of train | *A secret plan to murder an important person | A story about a castle | A friendly party for a leader
exercise: Which word means nearly the same as assassination? | Celebration | *Murder | Birthday | Journey
test: In the news: «The assassination of the mayor shocked the whole town.» What does assassination mean here? | A long speech | *The murder of an important person | A surprise party | A town festival
test: Which sentence uses assassination correctly? | I ate an assassination for lunch. | *Historians study the assassination that helped start a great war. | The assassination was a sunny day at the beach. | My assassination of the dog was a lovely walk.
exam: Which best describes an assassination? | *The murder of an important or famous person, usually for political reasons | A surprise gift for a famous person | A pleasant meeting with a famous person | A slow walk to school
